      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">MLPlatformAgentBench: Can coding agents optimize machine learning platform interfaces?</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="en">MLPlatformAgentBench: Can coding agents optimize machine learning platform interfaces?</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="sv">MLPlatformAgentBench â€“ Kan kodningsagenter optimera grÃ¤nssnitt fÃ¶r maskininlÃ¤rningsplattformar?</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">MLPlatformAgentBench â€“ Kan kodningsagenter optimera grÃ¤nssnitt fÃ¶r maskininlÃ¤rningsplattformar?</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="en">MLPlatformAgentBench â€“ Kan kodningsagenter optimera grÃ¤nssnitt fÃ¶r maskininlÃ¤rningsplattformar?</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="sv">MLPlatformAgentBench â€“ Kan kodningsagenter optimera grÃ¤nssnitt fÃ¶r maskininlÃ¤rningsplattformar?</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">
Coding agents are operating machine learning platforms, yet no systematic study has established which platforms they can operate, and at what cost. This thesis maps and measures that landscape.

A market assessment scores 39 machine learning platforms by whether an agent can manage feature, training, and inference pipelines through a Python software development kit, a command line interface, or a Model Context Protocol server. It also examines platform agents and platform meta-harnesses. Five platforms provide complete coverage through at least one of the first two interfaces, and three through both. One of those three is European. None provides full Model Context Protocol coverage.

MLPlatformAgentBench evaluates the interfaces on 22 tasks from feature engineering through operations, restricting each agent to one interface and basic shell tools. Across Hopsworks and Databricks, two American and two European models, two interfaces, and, for Claude, two skill conditions, coding agent and model choice made the largest performance difference. Claude Opus in Claude Code solved 98Â¢% of runs, compared with 36Â¢% for Mistral Large in Mistral Vibe. The interface changed how work was done, not whether it succeeded. When the command line interface and software development kit were similarly mature, progressive disclosure offered no measurable advantage. Also, skills had no detectable effect on Claude Code's accuracy. Operating platforms differed detectably in accuracy only for Mistral Large in Mistral Vibe, which was more accurate on Hopsworks. The Hopsworks configuration also used fewer turns, less local time, and lower Claude model invocation cost, but the design does not isolate platform from execution period and coding agent version. The mean Claude run cost 1.06 against 2.32 US dollars. Claude Code then produced six optimized command line interface variants and one optimized set of skills for each optimization. None beat its corresponding baseline. This null result supports treating agent-based interface optimizations as hypotheses requiring paired measurement.
</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="sv">
Kodningsagenter anvÃƒÂ¤nder maskininlÃƒÂ¤rningsplattformar, men ingen systematisk studie har faststÃƒÂ¤llt vilka plattformar de kan anvÃƒÂ¤nda och till vilken kostnad. Denna avhandling kartlÃƒÂ¤gger och mÃƒÂ¤ter detta landskap.

En marknadsbedÃƒÂ¶mning poÃƒÂ¤ngsÃƒÂ¤tter 39 maskininlÃƒÂ¤rningsplattformar utifrÃƒÂ¥n om en agent kan hantera funktions-, trÃƒÂ¤nings- och inferenspipelines via ett Python-programvaruutvecklingskit, ett kommandoradsgrÃƒÂ¤nssnitt eller en Model Context Protocol-server. Den undersÃƒÂ¶ker ocksÃƒÂ¥ plattformsagenter och plattformsmeta-harnesses. Fem plattformar ger fullstÃƒÂ¤ndig tÃƒÂ¤ckning genom minst ett av de tvÃƒÂ¥ fÃƒÂ¶rsta grÃƒÂ¤nssnitten, och tre genom bÃƒÂ¥da. Ett av dessa tre ÃƒÂ¤r europeiskt. Ingen ger fullstÃƒÂ¤ndig Model Context Protocol-tÃƒÂ¤ckning.

MLPlatformAgentBench utvÃƒÂ¤rderar grÃƒÂ¤nssnitten pÃƒÂ¥ 22 uppgifter frÃƒÂ¥n funktionsutveckling till drift, och begrÃƒÂ¤nsar varje agent till ett grÃƒÂ¤nssnitt och grundlÃƒÂ¤ggande skalverktyg. FÃƒÂ¶r Hopsworks och Databricks gjorde tvÃƒÂ¥ amerikanska och tvÃƒÂ¥ europeiska modeller, tvÃƒÂ¥ grÃƒÂ¤nssnitt och, fÃƒÂ¶r Claude, tvÃƒÂ¥ fÃƒÂ¤rdighetsvillkor, kodningsagent och modellval den stÃƒÂ¶rsta prestandaskillnaden. Claude Opus i Claude Code lÃƒÂ¶ste 98Â¢% av kÃƒÂ¶rningarna, jÃƒÂ¤mfÃƒÂ¶rt med 36Â¢% fÃƒÂ¶r Mistral Large i Mistral Vibe. GrÃƒÂ¤nssnittet fÃƒÂ¶rÃƒÂ¤ndrade hur arbetet utfÃƒÂ¶rdes, inte huruvida det lyckades. NÃƒÂ¤r kommandoradsgrÃƒÂ¤nssnittet och programvaruutvecklingspaketet var lika mogna, erbjÃƒÂ¶d progressiv avslÃƒÂ¶jande ingen mÃƒÂ¤tbar fÃƒÂ¶rdel. FÃƒÂ¤rdigheter hade inte heller nÃƒÂ¥gon mÃƒÂ¤rkbar effekt pÃƒÂ¥ Claude Codes noggrannhet. Operativplattformar skilde sig mÃƒÂ¤rkbart ÃƒÂ¥t i noggrannhet endast fÃƒÂ¶r Mistral Large i Mistral Vibe, vilket var mer exakt pÃƒÂ¥ Hopsworks. Hopsworks-konfigurationen anvÃƒÂ¤nde ocksÃƒÂ¥ fÃƒÂ¤rre varv, mindre lokal tid och lÃƒÂ¤gre kostnad fÃƒÂ¶r att anropa Claude-modellen, men designen isolerar inte plattformen frÃƒÂ¥n exekveringsperiod och kodningsagentversion. Den genomsnittliga Claude-kÃƒÂ¶rningen kostade 1,06 jÃƒÂ¤mfÃƒÂ¶rt med 2,32 amerikanska dollar. Claude Code producerade sedan sex optimerade kommandoradsgrÃƒÂ¤nssnittsvarianter och en optimerad uppsÃƒÂ¤ttning fÃƒÂ¤rdigheter fÃƒÂ¶r varje optimering. Ingen slog motsvarande baslinje. Detta nollresultat stÃƒÂ¶der behandling av agentbaserade grÃƒÂ¤nssnittsoptimeringar som hypoteser som krÃƒÂ¤ver parade mÃƒÂ¤tningar.
